      "snippet": {
        "text": "Since the public release of ChatGPT in November 2022, and the proliferation of generative AI tools that followed, there has been a significant research interest in the use of generative AI in education, including language education contexts. There is a growing body of scholarly work which has explored the potential and benefits of generative AI for language learners arguing that the use of generative AI holds significant potential and has positive effect on students' language learning (Agustini 2023;Lee et al. 2023;Toboula and Martinien 2023), reflexivity and critical thinking (Zhu et al. 2023;Tafazoli 2024), creativity (Creely 2024), intercultural communicative competence (Bonner et al., 2023), emotions (e.g. motivation, interest and engagement) (Ali et al. 2023;Mohamed 2024) and autonomy in language learning (Ali et al. 2023;Mohamed 2024). \n\nThere is also an emerging body of research that explores the potential of generative AI in language education, with the argument that generative AI can support language teachers 'to optimise their teaching effectiveness and better address the multifaceted needs of their learners' (Koraishi 2023, p. 56). One of the most commonly cited benefits of generative AI is its capacity to assist language teachers in creating resources such as lesson plans, assessment tasks and learning activities, saving teachers' time and effort (Jeon and Lee 2023;Koraishi 2023;Kohnke et al. 2023b;Law, 2024;Mohamed 2024). Generative AI can also be used to modify existing resources for differentiated learning (Kohnke et al. 2023b). Teachers have also been reported to use generative AI for marking and feedback on students' work (Jeon and Lee 2023;Han and Li 2024;Mohamed 2024). Han and Li (2024), for example, found that when undergraduate students received teacher comments that were based on feedback generated from ChatGPT, a broader range of aspects were included in the feedback and students incorporated more of these suggestions in subsequent drafts. The findings from this research highlight that collaboration between a teacher and generative AI resulted in more comprehensive and detailed feedback, enhancing learning opportunities for students.",
