      "snippet": {
        "text": "The impact of AI technology on the development and reform of education is profound and multifaceted. AI enables the creation of learning experiences tailored to individual student needs, preferences, and learning styles (Essa et al., 2023). By analyzing student data, AI algorithms can recommend specific learning materials, activities, and assessments that cater to each student's strengths and weaknesses. AI-powered adaptive learning platforms use machine learning algorithms to assess student performance in real-time, adjusting the difficulty level and pace of instruction accordingly (Gligorea et al., 2023). These platforms provide personalized learning pathways that adapt to students' progress, ensuring optimal learning outcomes. \n\nIntelligent tutoring systems leverage AI technology to provide individualized support and feedback to students. These systems can offer interactive lessons, practice exercises, and explanations tailored to each student's learning needs, enhancing comprehension and retention of educational content. AI enables educators and administrators to make data-driven decisions by analyzing large volumes of educational data. By leveraging predictive analytics and machine learning models, schools can identify trends, patterns, and insights that inform curriculum design, teaching strategies, and student interventions. \n\nAI automates routine administrative tasks like grading, attendance tracking, and scheduling, freeing up educators' time to focus on teaching and student engagement (Igbokwe, 2023). This automation improves efficiency, reduces workload, and enhances productivity in educational institutions. AI technology promotes accessibility and inclusivity in education by providing tools and resources that cater to diverse learning needs. Speech recognition software, text-to-speech applications, and assistive technologies support students with disabilities and ensure equal access to educational opportunities. \n\nAI offers opportunities for educators to enhance their professional development through personalized training programs, feedback mechanisms, and data-driven insights on teaching practices (Guan et al., 2020). Continuous learning platforms powered by AI support educators in improving their instructional skills and staying abreast of educational trends. AI-driven predictive analytics tools can forecast student performance, identify at-risk students, and recommend targeted interventions to support academic success. By analyzing student data and behavior patterns, educators can intervene early to address learning challenges and improve student outcomes.",
