      "snippet": {
        "text": "The integration of AI in education should not be viewed as a replacement for teachers; instead, it should be seen as a complementary tool that empowers educators to enhance their instructional practices. The collaboration between AI systems and teachers can create a synergy that harnesses the strengths of both, maximizing learning outcomes for students. By leveraging AI technologies, teachers can free up time from mundane administrative tasks, such as grading and data analysis, allowing them to focus on higher-order skills, personalized mentoring, and fostering creativity in the classroom. \n\nThis paper presents recent research to help understanding the role of artificial intelligence in education. This paper is organized as follows: in the first section are presented the education role for personal development. The educator's role in education is presented in the next section. After that, emmerges a discussion about educator that are only focused on on content, which we call content-centered-teachers. Next section is about the ai state of the art, which means that it is presented concepts about generative artificial intelligence for content generation. The main question about educator centered on content are at risk for disappearing is present in the next section. After all, some still preliminary conclusions in this field are presented.",
