      "snippet": {
        "text": "Generative AI (GAI) chatbots such as ChatGPT are poised to fundamentally change the work of teachers, and therefore teacher preparation programs are at the forefront of integrating the use of GAI in educational settings (MacDowell & Korchinsk, 2023). GAI is poised to change how teachers develop assessments, plan lessons, create word problems, and influence other components of teaching. For example, Chat-GPT may be used to grade student work and create progress reports for students. It can also translate information to facilitate communication with non-English-speaking students and parents (Trust et al., 2023), to determine the readability of text, to track and monitor student progress, and to provide feedback (Celik et al., 2022). Thus, it is essential that preservice teacher education programs incorporate the use of GAI chatbots, so that preservice teachers (PSTs) are prepared to use these technologies in productive and useful ways as they enter the teaching profession (Tate et al., 2023). Although GAI can be useful, it is imperfect, especially in mathematics (Wardat et al., 2023), and teachers, particularly PSTs, must be reflective about the output generated by chatbots such as ChatGPT. Tate et al. assert that GAI is \"fallible but useful\" (2023, p. 7). \n\nOne use of GAI is to generate lesson plans and to make suggestions regarding pedagogical approaches (Trust et al., 2023). Another use of GAI is to prompt it to solve mathematics problems, so that PSTs are aware of different possible solutions to the problems, although GAI is sometimes incorrect, performing at the level of an average graduate student (Frieder et al., 2024). Thus, using ChatGPT's output requires reflective analysis on the part of the user. Lesson planning is of particular interest, since researchers have found that PSTs have difficulty planning lessons (Cevikbas et al., 2024;Lim et al., 2018;Sahin-Taskin, 2017). Many PSTs first encounter the requirement to plan a lesson in a methods class, often through a microteaching experience.",
