      "snippet": {
        "text": "This study is a cross-sectional design. A longitudinal approach may yield even more distinct differences between ScriptBot and GenBot since the scripted, repetitive nature of the ScriptBot will be more pronounced. Future studies should therefore follow a longitudinal approach (at least four coaching sessions) before the outcomes measures are recorded. The long terms effects of AI chatbot coaching should also be investigated, specifically the permanence of the coaching effect several months after the chatbot usage stopped. The GenBot used generative AI only as an augmentation to a scripted coaching conversation. This was done to make the comparison between ScriptBot and GenBot easier and fair. Future research should also include a purely generative AI coaching chatbot that functions based on one single prompt without any predefined conversation scripts. This could also expose users to generative AI inconsistencies and \"hallucinations\" which could affect measures. Future studies should also include a control and human coach group to quantify the relative effects of using a coaching chatbot. Another limitation of this study is the self-report mechanism used to collect data of coaching outcomes. Capturing users' perceptions could include subjective biases. A more robust measure would be objective measures such as 360-degree feedback from others or behavioural or performance changes. Future research should therefore explore objective measures of coaching efficacy. The context awareness of generative AI in coaching chatbots may hold promise in promoting specific outcomes for specific audiences. Future studies should therefore also explore the use of generative AI in coaching chatbots in specific contexts such as wellness, career support, first-time graduates employees and in specific sectors such as education and health.",
